    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Using Corollary <a href="/tag/76592F" data-tag="76592F">4.2.1.3</a>, we may reduce to the case where $X$ and $Y$ are $\infty $-categories. We note that $\sCoNerve [X \star Y]$ is a correspondence from $\sCoNerve [X]$ to $\sCoNerve [Y]$. To complete the proof, it suffices to show that $\bHom _{\sCoNerve [X \star Y]}(x,y)$ is weakly contractible, for any pair of objects $x \in X$, $y \in Y$. Since $X \star Y$ is an $\infty $-category, we can apply Theorem <a href="/tag/BDB1F7" data-tag="BDB1F7">1.1.5.13</a> to deduce that the mapping space $\bHom _{\sCoNerve [X \star Y]}(x,y)$ is weakly homotopy equivalent to $\Hom ^{\rght }_{X \star Y}(x,y)$, which consists of a single point. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
